# Git keeps the files of this analysis project byte for byte: no line-ending conversion.
# The project's records hash the bytes of its inputs and scripts, so a checkout that turned LF into
# CRLF (or back) would show them as changed on another machine. Inside another Git repository this
# holds for the project's directory only, over that repository's own line-ending rules.
# Delete this file to let Git handle line endings as core.autocrlf or the enclosing repository's
# rules say.
* -text
